Options are ordinary R options under the \code{ezrsurvey.} prefix, so anything you
can do with \code{\link[=options]{options()}} works here too, and a setting lasts for the session.
Reading (\code{ezrsurvey_options()} with no arguments) returns every recognised
option's current effective value; setting returns the previous values
invisibly, so you can restore them. To make settings permanent, write them to
a YAML profile -- edit it with \code{\link[=edit_ezrsurvey_profile]{edit_ezrsurvey_profile()}} or dump the current
session with \code{\link[=save_ezrsurvey_profile]{save_ezrsurvey_profile()}} -- which is loaded automatically at
package start-up.
